34,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The suspended bay has a weight limit of four hundred kilos per square metre, and the evening hire bookings mean we have to deal with caterers and chairs moving through the gallery.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Interestingly, the data shows that visitors are more likely to return when there is a mechanism running or a display that changes, rather than just cased objects.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The conservation lab is really struggling with only one person, and there's a huge backlog of two hundred pieces waiting to be cleaned! Also, most of our volunteers are from the town history circle.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"I found out that loan transport costs are eating up nearly a third of our installation budget, and two of the last four openings were delayed because of late lender paperwork!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears our budget is being quietly consumed by bespoke mount-making and rising joiner rates, while powered displays have required seventeen call-outs last season alone, some during public hours.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Benjamin, those call-outs for powered displays sound worrying, especially if they happen while the gallery is open. It seems like a lot of disruption for the visitors.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Rin, the fact that visitors value seeing someone working or talking suggests that a static exhibition might not be the most effective choice for the main gallery.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Rin,,"That's a great point, @Toshio! Maybe we should pick something where people can actually see the work happening, since the visitors like that so much!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, if transport costs are that high and paperwork is causing delays, maybe we should avoid exhibitions that rely too heavily on loans from far-away places.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"I quite agree, Kenji. It would be prudent to favor a proposal that minimizes external dependencies and avoids the exorbitant costs of international couriers and bespoke mounting.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Rin, if the conservation lab is already so backed up, we should probably avoid any exhibition that requires a lot of new cleaning or stabilization work.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Daisuke, that is a very sensible observation. We must ensure the exhibition we choose does not place an impossible burden on our already strained conservation staff.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I'll keep that in mind! We definitely shouldn't make the one person in the lab even more stressed, or they might just disappear!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, if people like things that move or change, but we need to avoid high transport costs and delays, we should look for something local but dynamic.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely, Kenji. A local focus would mitigate the shipping risks and costs, while a dynamic element would satisfy the public's appetite for engagement without necessarily requiring complex, high-maintenance machinery.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I also hope we consider the evening hire bookings; we should avoid anything too fragile or impossible to move if caterers need to get through.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"That is a valid concern, Daisuke. We need a layout that is flexible enough to accommodate those events without risking damage to the exhibits.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I'll remember that! We need a plan that doesn't get in the way of the party chairs, or we'll have a big mess on our hands!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I think we've all found some really important warnings. We need a show that's local, doesn't break the bank, and won't get in the way of the catering!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed. We have established a clear set of constraints: low transport costs, minimal conservation needs, structural awareness, and a preference for interactive or human elements. I believe we are now ready to evaluate the candidates.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
55,3,,status,Kenji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
