57,3,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
58,3,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The candidates are Textiles of the Region, Maritime Trade Routes, City Under Excavation, and Light and Motion. I think Textiles of the Region seems safest for the floor and the evening hires.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Textiles of the Region also aligns with the visitor data, as it includes demonstration sessions with craftspeople, which provides the human element people enjoy.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I like Textiles of the Region too! It has those interviews and demonstrations, and it sounds like it wouldn't need the conservation lab to do too much work.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Maritime Trade Routes sounds like it would have too many loans and paperwork headaches, and Light and Motion seems like it would be a nightmare for the maintenance log. I'm with you all on Textiles!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"I concur. Textiles of the Region avoids the logistical pitfalls of Maritime Trade Routes and the maintenance burdens of Light and Motion, while remaining fiscally responsible. It is the most logical choice.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I'm just wondering about City Under Excavation; wouldn't a working conservation bench be too much for the one person in the lab, as Rin mentioned?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"That is a sharp observation, Daisuke. Adding a public-facing bench to an already overwhelmed lab would likely be counterproductive and stressful for the staff.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Rin,,"Yeah, that would be way too much pressure! The poor person in the lab would have people staring at them while they're trying to catch up on two hundred pieces!","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"Exactly! Plus, ""excavation"" sounds like it might involve heavy stones, and @Daisuke mentioned the weight limit for the suspended bay. Textiles is definitely the way to go.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed, the risk of exceeding the structural capacity with heavy archaeological finds is a concern we cannot ignore. Textiles of the Region remains the most prudent and appealing option.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I feel confident now. I will vote for Textiles of the Region.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"I agree. Based on the visitor preferences and the logistical constraints, I vote for Textiles of the Region.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'm voting for Textiles of the Region too! It's the most fun and the kindest to the staff!,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm voting for Textiles of the Region as well! It's the safest bet for our budget and our schedule.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I shall cast my vote for Textiles of the Region as well. It is the only candidate that satisfies our financial, structural, and staffing requirements while promising public engagement.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
